    "fold-lane-D-0929: folded the daOwl_c_classInit registry factory (0x02136798..0x021367e8) into this already-promoted TU, widening the complete delinks.txt claim from 0x02135700..0x02136798 to 0x02135700..0x021367e8. The loose one-function source hand-called fBase_c::operator new(1016) + the inherited dEnemyBase_c ctor + this class's vtable store + four member subobjects in field order (dCcAcPos_c, dBgCh_Actr, ModelAnim, dExtShadowModel_c); daOwl_c has no user-declared constructor, so `new daOwl_c()` reproduces the identical sequence with zero mangled calls. This TU keeps #pragma defer_codegen off, so emission follows source order (ROM-ascending); the factory appends after InitResources. tools/tubuild.py verify reports 22/22 MATCH, objisolate clean, reloc-destinations clean, TEXT-VERIFIED, with no new compiler_only_output needed (the existing _ZN7daOwl_cD2Ev deadstrip row, from the out-of-line destructor, already covers the homeless base-object-destructor helper `return new` emits here). Retired: src/d_a_owl.c (credited tangosdev, carried into attribution.json as a path#symbol override).",
